---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Card from '../components/Card.astro';
import CardGrid from '../components/CardGrid.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Papers"
  description="The six UniDPP contribution papers to ISO/IEC JTC 5 and partner bodies: the framework position paper, registry requirements, lifecycle and events, the implementation report, the trust annex input, and the terminology announcement — with PDFs."
  eyebrow="Contributions"
>
  <h1>Papers and contributions</h1>
  <p class="lede">
    Six planned contributions to ISO/IEC JTC&nbsp;5 and partner bodies, submitted through the
    secretariat and liaison channels as N-documents. ISO values implementation experience;
    the implementation report publishes conformance and drift findings alongside the
    position work.
  </p>

  <section id="catalogue" class="plate" aria-labelledby="catalogue-h">
    <h2 id="catalogue-h">Catalogue</h2>
    <CardGrid>
      <Card title="An international framework for the Digital Product Passport" tag="Position paper">
        <p>
          CalConnect + TC 154 + OIML + ELF co-branded. The fourteen invariants, the lens
          model, and the profile mechanism. Submitted as a liaison contribution under
          agenda item 11/13.
        </p>
        <p class="paper-links">
          <a href="/papers/an-international-framework-for-the-dpp.pdf">PDF</a>
        </p>
      </Card>
      <Card title="Semantic registry requirements" tag="Technical contribution">
        <p>
          TC 154 + Enosema + UN/CEFACT. Fills the EN 18223 §4.3 vacancy; FERIN / ISO 19135
          governance; UNTDED seed. Workstream B / C input.
        </p>
        <p class="paper-links">
          <a href="/papers/semantic-registry-requirements.pdf">PDF</a>
        </p>
      </Card>
      <Card title="DPP lifecycle, events and validity" tag="Technical contribution">
        <p>
          CalConnect. The fifteen-event post-sale taxonomy and the EN support matrix; ISO
          8601 and ISO 34000 citations. Workstream B input.
        </p>
        <p class="paper-links">
          <a href="/papers/dpp-lifecycle-events-validity.pdf">PDF</a>
        </p>
      </Card>
      <Card title="UniDPP: a reference implementation of the international framework" tag="Implementation report">
        <p>
          UniDPP / CalConnect. Architecture, EU-profile conformance results, drift findings
          against the EN texts, and a benchmark against freeDPP and OpenDPP.
        </p>
        <p class="paper-links">
          <a href="/papers/unidpp-reference-implementation.pdf">PDF</a>
        </p>
      </Card>
      <Card title="Cross-recognition trust for DPP" tag="Trust annex input">
        <p>
          CalConnect + TC 154, OIML co-sign. The SIGNATIF DPP annex as workstream D input;
          CNML as the ESDC realization.
        </p>
        <p class="paper-links">
          <a href="/papers/cross-recognition-trust-for-dpp.pdf">PDF</a>
        </p>
      </Card>
      <Card title="The DPP vocabulary dataset" tag="Terminology announcement">
        <p>
          CalConnect. The Glossarist browser URL with Form 4 attached (NWIP-1). The
          vocabulary draft is generated from the dataset.
        </p>
        <p class="paper-links">
          <a href="/papers/dpp-terminology-dataset.pdf">PDF</a>
        </p>
      </Card>
      <Card title="The DPP that works at every border" tag="Delegate explainer">
        <p>
          Two pages for the JTC 5 delegate: the one-sentence claim, the ePassport
          precedent, and the five-beat talk track. The back page carries a QR to
          this site.
        </p>
        <p class="paper-links">
          <a href="/papers/dpp-works-at-every-border.pdf">PDF</a>
        </p>
      </Card>
    </CardGrid>
    <p class="meta">
      Sources and revision history:
      <a href="https://github.com/unidpp">the unidpp repositories</a>; the PDFs above are
      the current revision, served from this site.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="nwips" aria-labelledby="nwips-h">
    <h2 id="nwips-h">New work item proposals</h2>
    <p>
      Four proposals carry the work into ISO/IEC JTC 5, with Forms 4 drafted from the plan
      and the audit evidence:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>NWIP-1</strong> — ISO 25534-1 Part 1 (Vocabulary): 80–120 entries with a
        harmonization annex across EN, UNTP, ISO 59040, and 25534-1.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>NWIP-2</strong> — semantic definitions and data element registry: FERIN
        federated registers per ISO 19135, identifiers per ISO/IEC 15459, UNTDED seed,
        OpenCDD technology.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>NWIP-3</strong> — lifecycle, events and validity: the E1&ndash;E15 event
        taxonomy, the status state machine, the temporal profile of ISO 8601, and the
        archival model.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>NWIP-4 (flagship)</strong> — the profile mechanism for multi-jurisdictional
        operation: profiles as registered, versioned, signed lenses on one identity;
        three-axial composition; sovereign crypto suites co-signed on one payload.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      The evidence the papers rest on is public: the
      <a href="/implementation/conformance/">EU-profile conformance register</a> (paper 4's
      results annex) and the <a href="/implementation/demos/">demonstration runs</a>.
    </p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .paper-links {
    margin: 0.7rem 0 0 !important;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.78rem;
  }
  .paper-links a {
    color: var(--accent);
  }
</style>
